        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Begin with the landscape",
        "content": "Iran’s outdoor environments call for different ways of looking and travelling. Damavand, a volcano in the Alborz range of northern Iran, supports hiking, climbing, and skiing. The southeastern Lut Desert presents another setting: wind-eroded ridges, stony surfaces, and accumulated sand. These are distinct physical environments rather than interchangeable backdrops for an outdoor holiday. [s1][s2]\n\nA useful starting question is therefore what an excursion involves: observing a landscape, travelling through it, or attempting a demanding objective. A mountain photograph does not establish the difficulty of a route, just as a photograph of dunes does not describe an entire desert. The pages in this branch separate activities so that their terrain, knowledge requirements, and evidence can be considered individually.",
