        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Preparation and an established outdoor culture",
        "content": "Mountaineering is also part of Iranian recreational life. Naturefriends International describes urban residents travelling to the mountains on weekends and reports cooperation between Austrian and Iranian mountaineering organizations. Its account records the establishment of a Naturefriends group in Iran in 2018 and a training seminar near Damavand in March 2019. These are documented examples of cooperation, rather than evidence that every operator or outing meets a common standard. [s5]\n\nThe UIAA’s expedition-planning guidance emphasizes knowing the itinerary, understanding alternatives if weather or injury intervenes, checking equipment, and establishing how emergency services could be contacted. It presents written guidance as support for skills developed through training. For readers evaluating an excursion, these subjects offer useful questions about how the trip is organized; they do not establish the availability of rescue or communications in a particular place. [s6]",
