        "heading": "Activity choice and conservation",
        "content": "Adventure travel can affect the landscape that attracts visitors. In its 2016 evaluation of the Lut Desert, the International Union for Conservation of Nature identified damage associated with unregulated vehicle excursions, campsites, and tourism. That historical assessment makes an important distinction: reaching a remote landscape and protecting its features are separate management tasks. It does not establish which activities or routes are authorized today. [s7]\n\nThis branch includes desert exploration, mountaineering, caving, nature walks, mountain biking, and boating and marine activities. The present overview establishes mountain and desert context most securely. Its remaining activity branches require additional specialist and local evidence before this can serve as a comprehensive guide. Read the focused pages as explanations of their subjects, and obtain separately verified operational information before treating any description as an itinerary.",
